# Shell scripts run on the Linux server. Git was checking them out with CRLF
# on this Windows machine, which makes a committed script unusable there: the
# carriage return becomes part of the interpreter path and the kernel answers
# 'bad interpreter: no such file or directory'. Pin them to LF.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Migration .sql files are deliberately NOT pinned here. Prisma stores a
# checksum of each applied migration, and production already holds the
# checksums of the CRLF copies this working tree uploaded. Re-encoding them
# would make the next `prisma migrate deploy` reject every applied migration
# as modified. See audit/AUDIT_2026-10-28_FULL_PASS.md.
